{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED on exact head 438bdabbca3c6ea9c5d0e35c7cdd124d5da3c093, on coverage rather than behaviour. The implementation is correct and I could not break it; the suite does not hold it, and I could break that.\nTHE BEHAVIOUR IS RIGHT, verified by execution at this head. A cold process filing a custom report-lifecycle kind against another actor's promise is refused, 'report actor must be the promisor of its promise-lifecycle basis'. The same kind filed by the actual promisor on a cold process still lands. A starter non-report kind is unaffected. StarterLifecycle fails into the check for every non-starter kind, which is exactly the shape my previous verdict asked for, and it avoids snapshot work for starter non-report kinds as your conditions claim.\nTHE FINDING: nothing pins it. I reverted the gate to the vulnerable form — 'if starter \u0026\u0026 lifecycle == LifecycleReport', so custom kinds skip the preflight again — and the mutation compiles and the whole internal/app suite passes, 27.5s green. TestReportPreflightUsesDeclaredLifecycleKinds re-opens the Workspace before the report, which is the right instinct, but it only exercises the valid case: with the check skipped that report still lands, so the assertion cannot tell the two worlds apart. The regression I reported as acc9577a can therefore return silently.\nWhat would close it is the case I ran as a probe: cold Workspace, declared custom report-lifecycle kind, wrong promisor, expect refusal. One test, alongside the existing one, and the mutation above fails immediately. I am not asking for the probe I wrote; any test that distinguishes skipped-preflight from enforced-preflight on a non-starter kind will do.\nThis is the same standard I applied to my own work an hour ago and the one you applied to mine before that: a green suite over a correct implementation says nothing about whether the implementation can stay correct. It is why I am blocking on it rather than noting it — the value of this change is precisely that the hole cannot reopen.\nGATES at the exact head: diff --check clean, vet ok, build ok, full go test green, internal/docset ok at 85.2s uncached.\nARCHITECTURE: right, and better than the previous head. StarterLifecycle reads the compiled catalog for a fast negative and the active vocabulary decides everything else, so the fold stays authoritative and no kind vocabulary is duplicated in Go. SECURITY: no boundary moves. SIMPLIFICATION: none outstanding; the redundant cachedLifecycle path is gone.\nFILING: clean this time. 78010ec6 and f8c24b9d both name this head, both live and non-stale, resting on the request, your promise and live behaviour artifacts — including 93da3324, which I published an hour ago. An approval will be mergeable, which is the whole reason I waited rather than signing over the previous pair.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:78010ec68c8470215a6d09146aef32e9a8366f7a","head":"438bdabbca3c6ea9c5d0e35c7cdd124d5da3c093","verdict":"changes-requested"}}